{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he fashioned it.</b> It refers to gold — the meaning is that of binding silver, as in ״ויצר ככרים כסף בשני חריטים״ (he fashioned silver ingots in two molds), and in Old French, gadleish." "<b>And he made it into a calf.</b> And not any other creature, because the mixed multitude began the transgression. And it is written ״זה אלי ואנוהו״ — for Israel saw the Shekhinah, but the mixed multitude saw only the feet of the ministering angels that were beneath the throne, which were like the foot of a calf. They thought these were the footsteps of the Holy One, blessed be He. And that is what is written in Psalms: ״ראו הליכותך״ etc. ״ועקבותיך לא נודעו״ — for they thought from the footprints of the angels that they were the footprints of the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>And they said: These are your Elohim, O Israel.</b> Were they fools, to say that this calf, made today from gold, brought them out of Egypt? Rather, we find sorcerers, terafim, ovot, and yiddim in which there is a spirit of impurity, and they supposed that in this [calf] there was a spirit of purity, and therefore they said: These are your Elohim, O Israel. And in order to test His creatures before the attribute of mercy, the Holy One, blessed be He, gave power to the spirit of impurity, as we find: ״כי יקום בקרבך נביא ונתן לך אות או מופת ובא האות והמופת״ etc. ״כי מנסה HaShem Elohimיכם אתכם״ etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The Old French gloss גדל״‎ש is obscure; it may relate to melting or casting metal."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:31.590556510Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}